  "id": "Compound::DB00966 - Gene::1244",
  "verbalization": "Telmisartan, a member of the angiotensin II receptor antagonists, is linked to Abcc2 through a shared pathway involving Eprosartan. The evidence suggests that Telmisartan and Eprosartan both bind to the same biological target, Abcc2, and that Eprosartan is implicated in the development of arthritis, which is a downstream effect of Telmisartan. This implies that Telmisartan may exert its effects on Abcc2 through a mechanism that is indirectly mediated by Eprosartan. The lowest common ancestor of Telmisartan and Eprosartan is the angiotensin II receptor antagonist class, which provides a common biological context for their interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Abcc2 in the pharmacological actions of Telmisartan, particularly through the involvement of Eprosartan as a mediator.",
